    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1747">

                <pb facs="1273" n="1157" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.74/72.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 555.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 12, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my despatch No. 458 of March
                    31, 1915, reporting that the Secretary of Foreign Relations had stated to me
                    that the Director of the London International Radio Convention had requested the
                    transmission to him of the rules and regulations adopted by Panama with
                    reference to wireless telegraphy and wireless stations within its jurisdiction,
                    I have the honor to report that, after twice asking at opportune times Señor
                    Lefevre for a copy of said communication and his promising to send it, I have
                    received a note from him stating that the Secretary of Government and Justice of
                    Panama had answered said Director <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush">that the rules adopted are the same that have force in
                            the United States of America by reason of them having taken charge,
                            according to the convention celebrated with Panama, for the service of
                            wireless communication.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>A copy of said note and its translation are enclosed.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Jennings Price.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d1747-a1.xml" xpointer="d1747-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
